# Fixed network IPs (Pi5)

Do **not** change these addresses unless the user explicitly asks:

| Interface | Role | Fixed IP | NM connection |
|-----------|------|----------|---------------|
| `eth0` | L2 lidar link | `192.168.1.2/24` | `Wired connection 1` (`never-default`) |
| `wlan0` | LAN / MyView | `192.168.1.61/24` | `CU_LONGQR_5G` (company) or `mesh61` (mesh) |
| L2 device | Unitree lidar | `192.168.1.62` (default) | - |
| MyView PC | Scheduler | usually `192.168.1.100` (`.env` `MYVIEW_SERVER_URL`) | - |

Related env: `PC_IP=192.168.1.2` (means Pi eth0 as seen by L2, not the WiFi IP).

Authoritative config: NetworkManager `system-connections` only.
Keep cloud-init network disabled (`/etc/cloud/cloud.cfg.d/99-disable-network-config.cfg`).
Do not put static IPs back into `dhcpcd.conf`.
WiFi: both `CU_LONGQR_5G` and `mesh61` may autoconnect (equal priority 80; `auto` picks stronger SIGNAL).
Manual switch: `scripts/switch-wifi-env.sh company|mesh|auto|status`.
Watchdog respects `/var/lib/wifi-env/desired`.

Do not rewrite host NetworkManager / netplan / dhcpcd for WiFi hardening unless the user explicitly requests it and accepts downtime risk.
